  "prior_attempts": [
    "The first QN90A round completed acquisition/public operations and cleanup but the observer missed native processes because proc exposed their private bind as /worker. Its timings and logs remain private; it did not qualify native resource coverage.",
    "The initial S90D migration request was explicitly rejected before launch: a completed native task already occupied that coordinator. Its original managed fixture and observer were reconciled and cleaned, with rescue unfired. The guard was retained; a service relaunch reset the task before a fresh trial.",
    "A QN90A visibility investigation tried an unsupported read-only public status operation, which was rejected. The committed native transaction was resumed only for remaining measurements/normal return/cleanup; migration was not replayed. Read-only mapped-executable evidence established /worker and the exact signed digest.",
    "S90D probe cleanup encountered a disappearing proc mountinfo entry and stopped before deletion. It completed only after reconciling ownership and proving failing proc entries absent or terminal.",
    "Service relaunch preparation preserved enrollment, retained jobs and selection on each boot. QN90A changed hosting PID; S90D reset the native task and worker while reusing its WRT hosting PID. Spent launch timers and independent rescues were retired and unfired."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "One integrated round and two command/job samples per profile are not a performance or tail distribution. Native-default, no-regression and endurance gates remain open.",
    "Native service acquisition still uses the managed capability/mount entry bridge. Enable-to-ready is observed through 200 ms status polling and includes scheduling; it is not .NET-free startup or a controlled power cycle.",
    "Host job/transfer timings include durable private journaling, new TLS connections for job requests, status polling, and client checksum/fsync work. Individual RPC times exclude the surrounding journal writes; transfers use pinned keep-alive sessions.",
    "The observer has roughly 10 MiB of buffers and nonzero sampling/CPU cost. Its resources are reported separately but can affect worker scheduling and pressure.",
    "One-second sampling captured exact selected native worker/guardian identities repeatedly, but is not exact process-tree peaks, wakeups or complete acquisition-process coverage. QN90A had no entry-process sample; S90D had one candidate sample. Short-lived descendants can be missed and exited-child CPU is excluded.",
    "Per-role resource summaries span the captured lifetime of that identity, not only a single public operation. Managed-before and native lifetimes differ; do not compare CPU deltas as equal-work benchmarks.",
    "S90D native root admission again exceeded one second; managed app through-forget also exceeded one second. Continuous kernel/resource evidence is retained but does not identify the cause. Literal error scans are not a comprehensive error detector.",
    "No package deployment, reboot, standby, global policy, persistent capability or SMACK change was issued. Raw device paths, identities, kernel records and request receipts remain private."
  ]
}
